<%--
Record_Author

Renders WHO wrote a record: an actor's printed name, hyperlinked to their profile when the
current viewer can reach one. The display half of the actor contract - the framework's
reference implementation of showing authorship, and the component every "Created by ..." /
"Updated by ..." line should use.

Args:
  $author (required, may be null) - the pair produced server-side by
      Rsx_Model_Abstract::get_created_by_author() / get_updated_by_author():
      {name: string, url: string|null}, or null for an unattributed record.

Content (optional) - what to render when $author is null. Defaults to "Unknown".
      Use it when the page knows something better: <Record_Author $author=x>System</Record_Author>.

WHY THE DATA COMES IN AS AN ARG. The name and the URL are BOTH server-side answers: the
name may belong to a soft-deleted actor, and the URL is resolved through the destination's
own auth gates for the current realm. There is deliberately no "look up the author of
record X" endpoint - that would be a new identity-lookup surface over arbitrary records.
The controller or fetch() that already loaded the record asks for the pair:

    $data['created_by_author'] = $record->get_created_by_author();

    <Record_Author $author=this.data.record.created_by_author />

A NULL url is not an error - it is the documented answer for "no profile page exists, or
you may not see it", and renders as plain text. A deleted actor renders IDENTICALLY to a
live one (no "(deleted)" marker): that is the actor contract. A screen that wants to mark
deleted authorship decorates it itself.

See: php artisan rsx:man actors
--%>
<Define:Record_Author tag="span">
    <%
        const _author = this.args.author || null;
        const _placeholder = (content() || '').trim();
    %>
    <% if (_author && _author.url) { %>
        <a class="Record_Author__link" href="<%= _author.url %>"><%= _author.name %></a>
    <% } else if (_author) { %>
        <span class="Record_Author__name"><%= _author.name %></span>
    <% } else if (_placeholder !== '') { %>
        <span class="Record_Author__unattributed"><%!= _placeholder %></span>
    <% } else { %>
        <span class="Record_Author__unattributed">Unknown</span>
    <% } %>
</Define:Record_Author>
